<section class="wrap" id="open-core" aria-labelledby="open-core-title">
  <p class="eyebrow">/ Open core</p>
  <h2 id="open-core-title">Free to use, modify and self-host.</h2>
  <p class="lead">The CLI, the Action and the engine adapters are open source and work on their own. A hosted layer is planned as the paid product.</p>
  <div class="split">
    <div>
      <h3>Available today, free</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><code>rpr</code> CLI and <code>reapr-core</code>: <a href="https://github.com/reapr-corp/reapr/blob/main/LICENSE.md">FSL-1.1-ALv2</a>, each release becomes Apache 2.0 after two years</li>
        <li>Engine adapters: <a href="https://github.com/reapr-corp/reapr/blob/main/crates/reapr-stryker/LICENSE">MIT</a></li>
        <li>GitHub Action: <a href="https://github.com/reapr-corp/run">MIT</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="later">
      <h3>Planned, paid, not built</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Hosted compute with warm workers</li>
        <li>A global cache of mutant results</li>
        <li>History and metrics across runs</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
